From 69767707da2331d92fb794371b80bb1b8c22b1f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:56:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/24] Phase B: add Mamba real byte layout metadata
 (cache_category, mamba_real_layout)

Per MIGRATION_PLAN.md Phase B, opens the controlled exception to the
_MambaPageViewEdit "opaque bytes" invariant: a quantization codec needs to
read conv_state/ssm_state with their own dtype/shape instead of the single
dtype the page-view edit exposes for addressing.

- group_view.py: new MambaSubStateWireLayout msgspec struct; EngineGroupInfo
  gains cache_category (three-state: attention/mamba/unknown, for codec
  dispatch) and mamba_real_layout ((conv, ssm) wire layout), appended after
  recurrent_state for wire compatibility with old payloads.
- kv_cache_group_edits.py: new MambaSubStateLayout/MambaRealLayout dataclasses
  and _MambaPageViewEdit.real_layout(), which reads MambaSpec.shapes/dtypes
  directly rather than trusting apply()'s single-dtype addressing view.
  Updated the class docstring: the opaque-bytes claim no longer holds
  unconditionally now that real_layout() exists.
- kv_cache_groups.py: _cache_spec_category()/_mamba_real_layout_wire() plus
  per-layer resolve/merge helpers, mirroring the existing
  _resolve_per_layer_recurrent/_merge_layer_recurrent pattern. Wired into
  create_engine_group_infos_from_vllm's EngineGroupInfo construction.

Confirmed via a background investigation that _MambaPageViewEdit (the
two-tensor [conv_state, ssm_state] list registration), not the newer
_MambaUnifiedViewEdit, is what actually fires for vLLM 0.26.0 Mamba/GDN
hybrid models (traced through gpu_model_runner.py's initialize_kv_cache),
so real_layout() was added there per the plan.

Tests: 13 new tests (real_layout byte-math, cache_category classification,
mamba_real_layout msgspec round-trip and wire-compat defaults, error paths
for wrong sub-state count / oversized bytes). All 44 tests in the three
touched test files pass; no regressions in the broader v1 suite (8
pre-existing failures in test_engine_driven_multi_group.py /
test_engine_driven_transfer_multi_group_server.py reproduce identically on
the unmodified sync-v0.5.5_kvweave base, confirmed via git stash).

