From cd0a1ef8b6c3999d15fcfc4010d71c3373ec1c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:49:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/24] Phase C: variable-length L1 support and
 double-quantization guard

Adds L1ManagerProtocol.is_variable_size() (True for the CPU/Device-DAX
pinned-DRAM tiers, False for GDS's fixed-size slab DMA) so callers can
fail fast before enabling variable-size L1 payloads like KVWeave
quantization.

Adds a generic is_lossy flag to register_serde_factory() instead of
hardcoding serde names, so StorageManager can detect any lossy L2 serde
(fp8, turboquant) without a name allowlist. StorageManager gains
mark_l1_kvweave_quant_enabled()/is_l1_kvweave_quant_enabled() as the
real (not just capability-based) signal that L1 quantization is on,
and _build_l2_adapter() now hard-rejects adding a lossy L2 serde once
L1 quantization is confirmed enabled, checked before constructing the
underlying adapter to avoid leaking it on rejection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
