From 9c1dd26f7de34d2119d71ff6f27f62167b6b4c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:59:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/24] Phase D: wire KVWeave quantization into the
 engine-driven transfer path

Per MIGRATION_PLAN.md Phase D, connects the KVWeave codec (Phase A) and
Mamba real-layout metadata (Phase B) to EngineDrivenTransferContext's
register/submit_store/submit_retrieve, on both the sync and async paths.

- custom_types.py: new SerializedMemoryLayoutDesc (+ serialize/deserialize
  helpers) so a MemoryLayoutDesc can be embedded as a field inside
  RegisterEngineDrivenContextPayload (msgspec's torch.dtype/torch.Size
  codec hooks only fire for top-level RPC payload/response classes, not
  nested fields). Payload gains group_layout_descs (per-group SHM layout
  override for quantized groups) and enable_l1_kvweave_quant (declared
  intent). RegisterEngineDrivenContextResponse gains an error field so
  registration can be rejected instead of silently timing out.
- mq.py: MessageQueueServer._call_sync_handler gains a generic (not
  kvweave-specific) fallback -- if a sync handler raises and its response
  class is a dataclass with an `error` field, catch and return
  response_cls(error=str(exc)) instead of letting the exception vanish
  into the main loop's bare log-and-drop, which left callers seeing a bare
  timeout with no diagnostic.
- worker_transfer.py: GroupTransferPlan gains quantized/raw_layout_desc/
  quant_layout_desc/mamba_options, decided once per group in register() via
  new _decide_group_quantization() (attention: quantize iff smaller;
  Mamba: quantize iff within linear_max_size_ratio and mamba_real_layout is
  present; "unknown" category and MLA are never quantized). register()
  fail-fasts when quantization is requested but
  storage_manager.is_l1_variable_size() is false, and marks
  mark_l1_kvweave_quant_enabled() once confirmed (Phase C's guard, wired
  up here). submit_store/submit_retrieve route quantized groups' chunks
  through the codec's encode_chunk()/decode_chunk() via shared
  _encode_group_chunks()/_decode_group_chunks() helpers, reusing
  _select_group_chunks()'s selection so null/already-cached chunks are
  never quantized (R2).
- async_engine_driven.py: submit_store's background per-group gather loop
  gets the same quantization, sharing _encode_group_chunks() with the sync
  path (R3). Quantized groups skip the SHM direct-write branch (their slot
  is sized for the uint8 payload, not the raw tensor) and instead gather
  into pinned staging at the raw shape, encoding into a separate commit
  list after gather_done synchronizes.
- modules/engine_driven_transfer.py:
  register_kv_cache_engine_driven_context rejects enable_l1_kvweave_quant
  registrations against a fixed-size L1, and applies
  payload.group_layout_descs as a per-group layout override so quantized
  groups' SHM slots are sized in uint8 bytes instead of the raw KV dtype.
- kvweave_serde.py: encode_chunk/decode_chunk's public entry points now
  call _validate_cache_category_dispatch(), which rejects
  cache_category="unknown" unconditionally and any category/mamba_layout
  combination that doesn't uniquely determine the codec path (R1/R6 --
  the plan's most important negative-test requirement, guarding against
  the historical incident where a Mamba group's opaque page-view chunk
  shape happened to pass the attention codec's shape check).
- kvweave_config.py: MambaCodecOptions.conv_qkv_split is now resolved from
  {MODEL_PATH}/{MODEL}/config.json's text_config instead of being left at
  its placeholder default, and ssm_qbit's default changed from 16 to 4
  (per MIGRATION_PLAN.md 6.1, already validated in production).

Known gap (tracked for a follow-up commit, not fixed here): the sync
submit_store() path (worker_transfer.py, EngineDrivenTransferContext,
~line 1662) does not guard against passing a quantized group's SHM
out_buffers to gather_paged_kv_to_cpu(out=...). A quantized group's real
SHM slot is uint8-sized per quant_layout_desc, smaller than the raw KV
tensor gather writes into -- this is exactly the hazard
async_engine_driven.py's `if out_buffers is not None and not
plan.quantized` guard exists to prevent, but the sync path never got the
equivalent guard. test_submit_store_quantizes_only_selected_chunks's fake
out_buffers happens to be shaped like the raw tensor, so it doesn't catch
this. Must fix before Phase E (SHM + sync + quantized is a real deployment
combination).

Tests: new/updated coverage in test_kvweave_serde.py (R6 negative cases),
test_mq.py (_call_sync_handler error path), test_custom_types.py (payload/
response/layout-desc msgspec round-trips), test_engine_driven_multi_group.py
(_decide_group_quantization scenarios, selection-reuse on store/retrieve),
and test_engine_driven_transfer_multi_group_server.py (registration
fail-fast, layout override). tests/v1/multiprocess/ + tests/v1/distributed/
run 1882 passed / 25 failed, all pre-existing (missing native kvweave_quant
extension, or unrelated standalone-group issues) -- no new failures
introduced by this commit.

