From 23c44104be8a44e5ab412b32a50df943966b785e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:54:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/24] Fix SHM+quantized store: OOB gather write and lost
 encoded bytes

Per MIGRATION_PLAN.md Phase D's known-gap note (9c1dd26f), the sync
submit_store() path never guarded "quantized group + SHM direct write":
a quantized group's real SHM slot is sized for the uint8 payload
(quant_layout_desc), smaller than the raw KV tensor
gather_paged_kv_to_cpu(out=...) would write into.

Investigating the guard surfaced a deeper issue affecting both sync and
async paths: EngineDrivenContextShm.commit_store() unconditionally
ignores its chunks argument and sends b"" -- SHM mode assumes data is
already written into the slot during gather, commit only releases the
write lock. But quantized groups were gather-to-scratch -> encode ->
appended to the list passed to commit_store, so the encoded bytes were
computed and then silently discarded in SHM mode; retrieve would read
whatever garbage/stale bytes were already in the slot.

- worker_transfer.py: quantized groups now always gather into a fresh
  CPU buffer (avoids the OOB write), then in SHM mode copy_ the encoded
  uint8 bytes into the group's real slot (decode_chunk parses a
  self-describing payload, so the slot's un-touched tail from
  estimate_serialized_size's upper-bound sizing is inert); in pickle
  mode the encoded chunk is appended to cpu_chunks as before.
- async_engine_driven.py: same fix, plus a second bug this introduced:
  commit_target was a patched copy of gather_target, so a quantized
  group's range kept its raw un-encoded bytes even after copy_-ing the
  real encoded bytes into its SHM slot. Rebuilt commit_target per
  group_ranges entry instead, dropping SHM-quantized ranges entirely.
  Also fixed a related pinned-staging leak: the finally block released
  staging buffers only `if not used_shm_direct`, but quantized groups
  now stage even in SHM mode, so their buffers never returned to the
  pool. Switched to `if staged_chunks` and removed the now-dead
  used_shm_direct variable.
- test_engine_driven_multi_group.py: updated the two quantize-selection
  tests to use a realistic 1D uint8 SHM slot (not the raw float32
  shape) and assert the encoded bytes land in the slot with an empty
  commit list, instead of asserting on committed_chunks.

Tests: tests/v1/multiprocess/test_engine_driven_multi_group.py +
test_engine_driven_transfer_multi_group_server.py +
tests/v1/distributed/serde/test_kvweave_serde.py: 94 passed, 1
pre-existing unrelated failure (test_extra_tagged_group_is_standalone).
Full tests/v1/multiprocess/ + tests/v1/distributed/ regression not
re-run in this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
