From 841809ce0a81c532ab73d435a3adf1c8105f00a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:07:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] Fix R8-R10: per-group attention plane classification,
 chunk_shape rank, mamba slot over-reservation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

R8: attention quantization decision no longer uses a worker-wide
use_mla_flag polluted by Mamba tensor shapes; each group now classifies
its own EngineKVFormat into AttentionPlaneLayout (SPLIT_KV/FUSED_KV/
MLA/UNKNOWN) and dispatches accordingly.

R9: _group_chunk_shape() no longer inherits its rank from the
worker-level default_shape; it rebuilds dims from the group's own
group_use_mla_flag, fixing a ValueError crash for fused-K/V groups
whose worker default is split-K/V.

R10: _estimate_substate_quantized_size()/estimate_mamba_serialized_size()
no longer unconditionally reserve max(quantized_size, raw_size) per
Mamba sub-state. That was meant to cover the CONV_QUANT_ENABLED/
SSM_QUANT_ENABLED DEBUG toggles switching to a raw fallback at runtime,
but those flags are resolved once at registration and fixed for the
group's lifetime. ssm's raw fp32 size (~16.78MB) dominated the max()
over its quantized size (~2.1MB), so the L1 slot reservation barely
shrank despite quantization working correctly. Added quant_enabled
parameter to size exactly the branch encode_chunk() will actually take.

Verified via tests/v1/distributed/serde/test_kvweave_serde.py (20),
tests/v1/multiprocess/test_engine_driven_multi_group.py, and
tests/v1/multiprocess/test_mamba_quant.py: 106 passed.

See MIGRATION_PLAN.md §3.5 R8/R9/R10 for full investigation notes.
