From 8b8ee6d7f1e43ea2a2766277b79c92dae686013d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:46:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] kvweave: wire up native head-split kernel and fix
 num_threads config

- kvweave_config.py: add `_env_num_threads()` reading
  `LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_NUM_THREADS` (default 8) and wire it into
  `KVWeaveRuntimeConfig.from_env()`'s `attention_codec_kwargs`. This env
  var was referenced by deployment scripts but never actually consumed by
  `KVWeaveRuntimeConfig`, so the codec always ran the native quant kernel
  single-threaded (`num_threads=1`) regardless of the env var. Also bump
  `KVWeaveCodecConfig.num_threads`'s default from 1 to 8.
- kvweave_serde.py:
  - `_KVWeaveCodec.__init__`: default `num_threads` kwarg 1 -> 8, matching
    the config default above.
  - `split_fused_attention_heads` (used by `serialize_fused_tensor` and by
    the engine-driven store path's fused-K/V head-split scratch step): now
    calls the new native `kvweave_quant.kvweave_split_fused_heads` first
    (supports writing into a caller-provided `out=` scratch buffer),
    falling back to the previous ATen permute()/reshape()/copy_() only
    when the native extension or symbol is unavailable.
  - `deserialize_fused_tensor`: the per-head-scales merge step (undoing the
    head split after dequantizing) now prefers the new native
    `kvweave_quant.kvweave_merge_fused_heads`, with the same ATen-based
