From 4fb30744756482fd40e6a02a9b4d9a546c4229f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:46:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/24] xpu: simplify engine-driven KV transfer path

Add a compact block-ID SYCL kernel path backed by a persistent USM host buffer, avoiding token-slot expansion and unnecessary CPU-to-XPU copies. Simplify engine-driven store and retrieve processing to serial per-chunk transfers while retaining request-level async execution, and remove obsolete pipeline-depth controls and diagnostics.

Wire KVWeave thread configuration, update transfer benchmarks, and add focused XPU coverage for block-ID round trips and first-transfer behavior.
