From a190886f915aa34f9712a115594bb06e21bce6d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:03:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] xpu: fix NHD/HND address formula swap in fused-packed
 kernel, route attention format to native

submit_multi_layer_kernel_fused_packed had its HND and NHD page_offset
formulas swapped: the branch guarded by NL_X_NB_NH_BS_CS/_TWO_HS (HND,
physical layout [NB, NH, BS, CS]) used the NHD formula, and the NHD
default branch (NL_X_NB_BS_NH_CS, attention's fused K/V format) used
the HND formula. This silently gathered/scattered from the wrong
token/head offsets for any caller exercising the native SYCL path
with NHD data.

Swap the formulas back to their correct layouts, and split the loop
into two format-specific loops instead of branching per-element
inside a single loop: the NHD case now collapses to a single
loop-invariant base plus "+i" (no per-element div/mod), matching the
fused K+V kernel's shape. The HND case keeps its per-element head/
head_offset computation since head varies within the loop.

Verified via gather/scatter round-trip against a torch index_select
reference on real XPU hardware (Arc B390), across multiple shapes
including non-divisible head counts, for both NHD and HND, D2H and
H2D.

The bug previously went unnoticed because engine-driven transfer on
XPU unconditionally routed every format except the flash-infer layout
(NL_X_NB_TWO_BS_NH_HS, used by Mamba groups) to the torch_ops
fallback -- so the buggy NHD kernel path was dead code in production
despite compiling and linking cleanly. Add an explicit
_XPU_NATIVE_VERIFIED_FORMATS allowlist and route NL_X_NB_BS_NH_CS
(attention's NHD format) to the native kernel now that it's verified
correct. Other non-flash-infer formats stay on the torch fallback
until similarly verified -- this is an opt-in allowlist, not a
blanket re-enable.

Measured ~3.4x faster gather_paged_kv_to_cpu for the attention group
(0.68ms -> 0.20ms) on representative Qwen3.5-9B shapes (8 layers, 8
heads, head_dim=128).
---
 csrc/sycl/mem_kernels_sycl.cpp                | 58 ++++++++++++-------
 .../v1/multiprocess/transfer_context/base.py  | 15 +++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/csrc/sycl/mem_kernels_sycl.cpp b/csrc/sycl/mem_kernels_sycl.cpp
index 3b74e46e..d53af353 100644
--- a/csrc/sycl/mem_kernels_sycl.cpp
+++ b/csrc/sycl/mem_kernels_sycl.cpp
@@ -366,28 +366,44 @@ void submit_multi_layer_kernel_fused_packed(
           0, layer_id, token_id, xwords_per_token, num_tokens,
             num_layers);
 
-        for (int i = tid; i < xwords_per_token; i += num_threads) {
-          const int head = i / xwords_per_head;
-          const int head_offset = i % xwords_per_head;
-          int64_t page_offset;
-          if constexpr (format == EngineKVFormat::NL_X_NB_NH_BS_CS ||
-                        format == EngineKVFormat::NL_X_NB_NH_BS_TWO_HS) {
-            page_offset = static_cast<int64_t>(slot_idx) * block_size *
-                              xwords_per_token +
-                          static_cast<int64_t>(block_offset) *
-                              xwords_per_token + i;
-          } else {
-            page_offset = static_cast<int64_t>(slot_idx) * block_size *
-                              xwords_per_token +
