From d1ac2bf30a12a155604288be2a2f9309a97e966f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:47:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] xpu: pipeline engine-driven quantized store across KV
 groups

Rework the engine-driven SHM store path so device->host gathers overlap
with CPU-side split/quantize work across *all* quantized KV groups, and
harden the XPU block-ID staging used by those overlapped gathers.

Async engine-driven store (async_engine_driven.py)
- Replace the per-group launch_window/process_window loop with a
  cross-group depth-2 pipeline (_run_async_bounded_pipeline). Chunks of
  every quantized-SHM group are flattened into one ordered list of
  _BoundedStoreBatch items; batch i+1's D2H gather is enqueued on the
  copy stream before batch i is waited on, split and encoded, so group
  N+1's copy overlaps group N's CPU work even when each group has only
  one chunk (the common production case).
- Split per-batch work into _launch_shm_quantized_batch (allocate raw
  SHM scratch or pinned fallback, gather, record event) and
  _process_shm_quantized_batch (event sync, Mamba / fused-head split into
  pool scratch, encode straight into the durable SHM slot).
- _release_pending_batch frees an already-launched next batch's scratch
  and staging buffers when processing the current batch raises, so a
  failed store cannot leak pool scratch.

Sync engine-driven store (worker_transfer.py)
- Replace _store_shm_quantized_group_bounded with a cross-group pipeline
  (_run_bounded_store_pipeline): a dedicated single-thread gather
  executor runs _bounded_gather_stage (gather + synchronize into raw
  scratch) for batch i+1 while the caller runs _bounded_encode_stage
  (split + encode into the SHM slot) for batch i.
- _BoundedStoreBatch / _BoundedGatherResult carry per-chunk plan, slots
  and scratch ownership; a failed gather frees its own scratch before
  re-raising, and leftover in-flight gathers are drained on error.
- Group selection is computed once up front (groups_with_selections)
  before any gather is issued; the gather executor is shut down in
  close().

XPU block-ID staging (csrc/sycl/pybind_sycl.cpp)
- multi_layer_block_kv_transfer previously reused a single thread-local
  USM host buffer for block IDs. With overlapped async gathers, a later
  call could overwrite block IDs still being read by an in-flight kernel.
  Replace it with slabs of 8 buffers each; every submission records a
  queue barrier event and a buffer is only reused once that event has
  completed.
- mem_kernels_sycl.cpp: macro whitespace only.

Tests and benchmarks
- test_async_engine_driven_transfer_context.py: cross-group pipelining
  order and scratch release on mid-pipeline failure.
- test_engine_driven_multi_group.py: sync-path commit-exactly-once and
  encode-failure propagation without commit.
- bench_engine_driven_shm_timing.py: optional AsyncEngineDrivenTransferContext.
- test_xpu_engine_driven_first_transfer.py: --submit-store
  --async-engine-driven mode, a --copy-mode eu|memcpy gather option, and
  a reverse-group gather check that block IDs stay isolated across
  overlapped gathers.
- New XPU benchmarks: test_xpu_multistream_copy_benchmark.py (does a
  stream pool give D2H concurrency), test_xpu_eu_vs_memcpy_benchmark.py
  (EU gather kernel vs per-slice queue.memcpy), and
  test_xpu_copy_under_compute_load_benchmark.py (copy latency vs a
  concurrent matmul load).
