From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:09:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] Scale native encode threads up when few engine groups
 are pipelined

The bounded store pipeline only overlaps the current chunk's native
encode with the next chunk's D2H gather, never two chunks' encodes
concurrently. With few engine groups there's less cross-chunk CPU
parallelism opportunity within one submit_store call, leaving physical
cores idle that a single chunk's OpenMP encode could otherwise use.
