From ae08c77130441067e7fb0ccb4f638e240279d40d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:46:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] Support RH-aware Mamba direct codecs and reuse bounded
 store scratch

Mamba direct encode/decode:
- Add default-enabled CONV_DIRECT_QUANT and SSM_DIRECT_QUANT environment
  switches and document CPU, scaling, RH, and page-layout constraints.
- Quantize conv Q/K/V segments and SSM states directly from opaque pages;
  pass randomized-Hadamard precondition tensors to the native direct API.
- Support RH via native scratch, including two-plane SSM states, while
  retaining the no-RH fast paths and rejecting unsuitable direct layouts.
- Decode directly into caller-owned page buffers and write fallback
  substates independently, preserving mixed FP16-conv/FP32-SSM bytes
  without gathering a just-written direct substate back out of the page.
- Select decode paths from payload metadata independently of encode flags;
  preserve split/raw fallbacks for disabled quantization, 16-bit SSM,
  unsupported scaling, and plane-boundary alignment constraints.

Store pipeline and scratch lifetime:
- Share complete Mamba direct eligibility between the codec and transfer
  contexts so preallocated split scratch does not disable eligible paths.
- Skip Mamba pre-splitting when both states can encode directly in both
  synchronous and asynchronous SHM store entry points.
- Reuse per-group depth-2 raw scratch and depth-1 split scratch across
  bounded-store chunks; wait for pending gathers before releasing rings,
  including encode failures and sequential concurrency fallback.
- Skip fused-attention head-split scratch when its direct kernel is used.
- Keep normal diagnostics without adding TEMP-DEBUG logging.

Regression coverage and benchmarking:
- Cover direct-versus-split byte equality, RH/scaling combinations,
  two-plane layouts, alignment/straddling fallbacks, caller-owned outputs,
  and synchronous/asynchronous direct selection and scratch cleanup.
- Add real-SHM scratch-ring reuse, group isolation, and failure-recovery
  tests, plus fused-attention split-scratch dispatch coverage.
- Add a manual Qwen3-14B dynamic pin-memory benchmark comparing per-chunk
  and merged heap allocations against real SHM-backed chunks, reporting
  latency, effective bandwidth, and implied extra per-call overhead.

Validation:
- Focused codec/Mamba/scratch-ring/async suite: 172 passed, 1 deselected.
- Expanded suite including engine-driven transfer: 207 passed, 4 failed,
  11 errors. One failure is the existing lowercase 'xpu' regex versus
  uppercase 'XPU' error message (confirmed unchanged in HEAD); the other
  failures/errors report unavailable lmcache_native.TransferDirection.
- git diff --cached --check passed. Manual pin-memory benchmark not run.

Native direct RH bindings must be supplied by a compatible KVWeave native
extension; the companion native-library changes live in a separate repo
and are not included in this commit.

