From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:46:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] Fuse Mamba token rows and channel tiles across CPU
 codec configurations

Enable capability-gated no-RH per-token conv and two-plane SSM direct paths while preserving old-extension fallbacks and existing per-tensor behavior. Document row/tile scratch and retain native payload framing.

Add compatibility and reconstruction-quality matrices covering float32/float16/bfloat16, single/two-plane pages, token/channel scaling, RH on/off and 4/8-bit payloads. Cover production layouts, concurrent calls, malformed scales, bounded allocations and sync/async store routing.

Add a reproducible 24-configuration production benchmark reporting SSM and complete Mamba codec encode/decode times plus RMSE, relative L2, maximum absolute error and cosine similarity against unquantized inputs.

Validation: the staged tree exactly matches previously validated integration snapshot 7a5289db. GCC regression: 841 passed; Intel compiler matrix: 823 passed; Intel single-thread fused matrix: 685 passed. C++17 integration validation: 841 passed with scratch-ring tests first; two attention scratch-ring tests were order-sensitive in the initial run and passed independently. Native KVWeave fused-scaling extension is required for newly enabled paths.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
