From 0150ca5fcb9a5378171b93186a1b214f833afe0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:12:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] Fix raw hybrid KV transfers in engine-driven SHM path

Backport of the raw transfer fixes from sync-v0.5.5_vllm_0.31.0.  With
LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_LINEAR_QUANT_ENABLED=0 the Mamba groups are stored
raw, and the same code paths that crashed on vLLM 0.31 exist here:

- Unquantized groups sent no layout to the server, which then inferred
  an attention-shaped [num_layers, num_physical_slots, hidden] SHM slot.
  Mamba conv/SSM state is not laid out per token, so the slot was sized
  wrongly and the raw gather could write past it on the device
  (UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST).  Every explicit group now sends its
  real layout (raw layout for unquantized groups, quantized layout
  otherwise); attention-shaped inference remains only as the fallback
  for registrations without group info.
- Derive recurrent chunk geometry from the group's own tensors and
  resolve the raw dtype per group; validate raw gather/scatter shapes
  and dtypes before transferring.
- Raw Mamba store gathers through the same single-chunk SHM scratch as
  the quantized path and copies raw bytes into SHM without encoding
  (sync and async contexts).  Raw batches are serialized; only
  consecutive quantized batches keep depth-2 gather/encode overlap.
- Raw Mamba retrieve scatters one scratch chunk at a time with a
  per-chunk skip derived from live chunk positions (null-chunk mask)
  and keeps the SHM read lock until scatter completes.

The vLLM 0.31-only int8/padded-stride native transfer fallback is not
included: vLLM 0.26 exposes float Mamba views with page-sized strides.

Tests cover raw Mamba store/retrieve via scratch (skip 0/4/8, masked
prefix, copy/scatter failure cleanup), per-group layout registration
with linear quant disabled, server slot sizing, and raw recurrent page
round trips.

