From d336ddc0dc978fdd888e6f32ed08c1e18b2b9707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jilongw <jilong.wang@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:22:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Add full-attention quant switch and default KVWeave
 quant device to XPU

New option:
- LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_FULL_ATTENTION_QUANT_ENABLED (default true) gates
  quantization of every attention group (split-K/V and fused-K/V),
  symmetric to LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_LINEAR_QUANT_ENABLED.  When disabled,
  _decide_group_quantization returns unquantized for attention groups
  and they transfer raw; Mamba/linear groups are unaffected.  The
  existing split/fused attention debug switches still apply when it is
  enabled.  Read on the worker at registration; the server sizes SHM
  from the per-group layout the worker reports.

Default change:
- LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_QUANT_DEVICE now defaults to "xpu" instead of
  "cpu", so quant/dequant runs on the kvweave_quant_xpu SYCL kernels
  unless explicitly overridden.  Requires kvweave built with
  KVWEAVE_XPU=1; set LMCACHE_MP_KVWEAVE_QUANT_DEVICE=cpu to restore the
  previous behavior.

Tests:
- Extend the attention layout switch test to cover the new full
  attention switch for both split and fused layouts.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
